  "qualification_limits": [
    "The encoding matrix executes surrounding code and checks native operand boundaries without simulating the MPX instructions.",
    "QEMU limitation mode explicitly skips its addr32 memory/table, LOCK BNDMOV, register-check and initializing E9 defects. Skips are not passes.",
    "Native stack-default bytes and address transport are qualified; physical MPX faults, stack #SS delivery, RTM interactions and partial-fault behavior are not established by this record.",
    "Native operand accesses are not probed by ordinary loads, but compiler-owned frames still require separation from guest data for general lifting.",
    "NeverD strict lifting remains closed for the seven stateful MPX operations until original branch/fault ordering and the shared state bank are integrated.",
    "Other x86 continuation families and global completion remain open."
  ],
